{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.dtIndex_cannot_supply_amplitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.dtIndex_cannot_supply_amplitude","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTIndexAmplitudeE.lean#L184-L202","doc":"**THE SCOPE-(b) STRUCTURAL EXCLUSION (sorry-free; invariant cited: bar-parity + `char ≠ 2`).**\nThe nonzero anti-self-adjoint amplitude `E = C + σ B` that a genuine A=3 lift forces\n(`A3AntiSelfAdjointLift.amplitude_nonzero` supplies `hlift : C + σ B ≠ 0`) is **NOT** equal to\nany DT-invariant / 3d-index / graded-Euler value `(d : R)`, `d : ℤ`.\n\nThe DT datum is bar-even (`dtIndex_barEven`); `E` is bar-odd (`amplitude_barOdd`, derived from\nthe bar-even mass-face cross-term); a nonzero element cannot be both (`barEven_barOdd_eq_zero`).\nSo the DT-invariant / 3d-index / graded-Euler route — which produces integer Behrend counts —\n**cannot** supply the amplitude that hits `r*`.  The amplitude belongs to the bar-ODD\nresurgent-Stokes / DM q-cubic sector (`conj:qdifference-kernel-prolongation-symbol`), not the\nbar-EVEN DT-index sector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.amplitude_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.amplitude_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTIndexAmplitudeE.lean#L167-L180","doc":"**The anti-self-adjoint amplitude `E = C + σ B` is bar-ODD (sorry-free).**  From `C` bar-odd\n(`crossTermBarEven_imp_C_barOdd`), `B` bar-odd, and `σ` involutive (`σ (σ B) = B`):\n`σ(C + σ B) = σ C + B = −C + B = −(C + σ B)`.  `E` sits in the anti-self-adjoint /\nresurgent-Stokes-phase sector — the OPPOSITE bar-parity from any DT-index value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.crossTermBarEven_imp_C_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.crossTermBarEven_imp_C_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTIndexAmplitudeE.lean#L149-L165","doc":"**A bar-even mass-face cross-term forces the off-block `C` bar-ODD (sorry-free).**  The\nphysical mass / C1 face carries a **bar-even** Berezinian cross-term `t = B·D⁻¹·C`\n(`BerezinianSelfAdjointCrossTerm`; the parity of `r* = μ₃/c₃`).  With the branching datum\n`B` bar-odd (`σ B = −B`, `A3OffBlockDerivation.offBlockNum_bar_odd`) and the odd diagonal `D`\nbar-even (`σ D = D`, the bar-conjugate 1-dim blocks give `D = a + σ a`), applying `σ` to `t`\ngives `−B·D⁻¹·σ C = B·D⁻¹·C`; cancelling the nonzero `B·D⁻¹` yields `σ C = −C`.  So the\noff-block that produces a bar-even mass face is itself bar-odd. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.barOdd_ne_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.barOdd_ne_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTIndexAmplitudeE.lean#L138-L145","doc":"**A nonzero bar-odd element is not equal to any bar-even element (sorry-free).**  The general\nlimitative core: the bar-odd amplitude `E ≠ 0` cannot coincide with any bar-even quantity —\nin particular with any DT-index / graded-Euler value (`dtIndex_barEven`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.barEven_barOdd_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.barEven_barOdd_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTIndexAmplitudeE.lean#L128-L136","doc":"**Bar-even ∧ bar-odd ⇒ zero (sorry-free; invariant: `char R ≠ 2`).**  If `σ x = x` (bar-even)\nand `σ x = −x` (bar-odd) then `x = −x`, so `2·x = 0`; in a field of characteristic zero\n`(2 : R) ≠ 0`, hence `x = 0`.  The bar-parity sectors intersect only at `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.dtIndex_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.dtIndex_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTIndexAmplitudeE.lean#L116-L124","doc":"**A DT-index / 3d-index / graded-Euler value is bar-even (sorry-free).**  A Behrend-signed DT\ncount, a rotated 3d-index, or a graded Euler characteristic `χ = Σ_k (−1)^k dim(G)_k` is an\n**integer**; the bar involution (a ring homomorphism) fixes the image of `ℤ` in `R`\n(`map_intCast`).  So every such value is bar-even — it lives in the self-adjoint / real-π-phase\nsector, the same sector as the `≤ 1` self-adjoint branching factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.BarOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.BarOdd","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTIndexAmplitudeE.lean#L110-L112","doc":"Bar-odd: negated by the bar involution.  The anti-self-adjoint / `±i`-π/2-phase sector; the\nGGM decay (`sinh`) face and the resurgent-Stokes amplitude `E` live here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.BarEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DTIndexAmplitudeE.BarEven","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DTIndexAmplitudeE.lean#L106-L108","doc":"Bar-even: fixed by the bar involution.  The self-adjoint / real-π-phase sector; the mass /\nC1 (`cosh`) face and every integer-valued DT-index / graded-Euler characteristic live here. ","signatureChunk":0}]}